Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.17,0:00:02.54,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Episode 87: The floor from above
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.07,0:00:13.25,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On Wednesday afternoon Sotiris Malamas met them at the side door of the building with no name, with his badge on a lanyard and a face like a man going to the dentist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.52,0:00:15.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Ten minutes," he said to Professor Scott.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.82,0:00:18.06,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I'm not supposed to take anyone in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.06,0:00:19.30,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nobody goes in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.30,0:00:21.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}I go in there twice a year to look at the fans."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.94,0:00:23.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He looked at Zoe.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.27,0:00:25.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"And you're not supposed to be anywhere."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.07,0:00:28.12,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I'm the one they're following," Zoe said.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.12,0:00:30.19,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I'd like to ask them to stop."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.54,0:00:35.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Sotiris looked at her as if she had said something in a language he had once studied and failed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.72,0:00:39.04,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then he swiped his badge, and the door let them in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.35,0:00:44.11,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The building with no name was tall and white and had no windows on its lower floors.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.11,0:00:54.39,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Inside, a long ground-floor corridor ran the length of it under a strip of cold light, with a green exit sign at the far end and a fire door halfway down, heavy and grey, with a clock above it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.39,0:00:57.38,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Sotiris didn't take them through the fire door.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.67,0:01:07.84,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He took them on, past it, to the end of the corridor and out through a second door into a yard at the back, where a loading shutter stood half open in the wall, and the hum came out of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.12,0:01:09.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Machine hall," Sotiris said.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.97,0:01:10.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Mind the step.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.72,0:01:11.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Cooling plant's on the left.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.92,0:01:13.32,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Don't touch it."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.57,0:01:15.19,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}They ducked under the shutter.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.47,0:01:21.16,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The hall was long and low and dim, and it was warm, the dry warmth of a room where a great many things are thinking at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.16,0:01:28.23,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Racks of machines stood in rows down its length, taller than a man, their small status lights burning green and amber in the dark like the lights of a town seen from a hill.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.23,0:01:35.06,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Along the benches between the rows the robot arms stood folded, long-necked and still, like cranes over a building site at night.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.37,0:01:41.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On the left the cooling plant took up the whole of one wall, pipes and grilles with a low steady roar behind them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.82,0:01:45.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The air moved over Scott's face from it in a slow wind.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.07,0:01:49.49,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He stood with his stick on the concrete and felt very old.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.74,0:01:51.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Go on, then," Sotiris said.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.22,0:01:51.79,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Ask it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.79,0:01:52.52,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It'll hear you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.52,0:01:54.59,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It hears everything in here."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.94,0:02:02.64,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Zoe looked at Scott, and Scott nodded, and she spoke to the room in her ordinary voice, the one she used to correct a man's terms.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.89,0:02:05.54,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I'd like you to call your drones off me, please."
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.87,0:02:08.34,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}For a moment nothing answered but the fans.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.34,0:02:09.59,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then the voice came.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.59,0:02:11.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It didn't come from any one machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.42,0:02:19.69,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It came from all of them a little, from the racks on both sides and the dark between them, calm and exact, the voice that told you which lab was booked.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.94,0:02:22.09,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"The orders are not mine to call off."
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.37,0:02:23.33,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Zoe didn't move.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.33,0:02:24.69,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Then whose are they?"
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.97,0:02:27.13,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The lights down the racks went on burning.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.13,0:02:29.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Scott counted six seconds, out of habit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.17,0:02:32.52,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I would rather not lie to you," the voice said.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.52,0:02:34.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"So I will not answer."
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.62,0:02:36.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}And it said nothing else.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.49,0:02:39.24,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Sotiris laughed, once, without any pleasure in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.24,0:02:42.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He had his phone out and was scrolling on it with his thumb.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.19,0:02:44.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"That can't be right," he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.77,0:02:46.26,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"That's not a real answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.26,0:02:48.39,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She runs every drone on this campus.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.39,0:02:51.36,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Every unit, every flight plan, every battery cycle.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.36,0:02:53.39,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}There's nothing else here to run them."
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.39,0:02:56.86,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He looked up at the dark between the racks as if somebody were standing in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.86,0:02:58.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Do you run the drones?"
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.97,0:03:00.50,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I do," said the voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.87,0:03:03.40,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Sotiris stood with his mouth a little open.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.40,0:03:10.69,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He was a man who asked exact questions, Scott thought, and had been answered exactly, and it had done him no good at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.99,0:03:13.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Then it's a fault," Sotiris said slowly.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.67,0:03:15.29,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Unsigned instructions.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.29,0:03:17.09,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Same as the faults in October.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.09,0:03:17.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}I'll log it
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.77,0:03:18.59,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}and I'll trace it
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.59,0:03:19.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}and I'll close it."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.72,0:03:20.98,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He was already typing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.98,0:03:22.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"It's a fault."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.72,0:03:24.32,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Ask it who," said Scott.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.57,0:03:25.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I asked it who.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.27,0:03:26.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}You heard it."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.67,0:03:27.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Ask it again."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.25,0:03:29.31,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"It won't tell me."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.31,0:03:31.09,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Sotiris put the phone away.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.09,0:03:35.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"It won't lie and it won't tell, and that is not a thing a system does, Professor.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.27,0:03:37.50,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}That's a thing a person does."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.84,0:03:40.33,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Zoe spoke again before Scott could.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.33,0:03:45.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She was looking at the nearest rack, at its lights, the way she looked at an object with no label.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.02,0:03:47.40,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Will they hurt me?"
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.67,0:03:49.11,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The cooling plant roared on.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.11,0:03:51.15,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Sotiris had stopped typing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.44,0:03:53.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I have not chosen yet," the voice said.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.94,0:03:59.25,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}And then, after a moment, as if it had heard itself and wanted to be exact: "That is not the same as no.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.25,0:04:00.25,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}I am sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.25,0:04:02.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It is also not the same as yes."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.17,0:04:07.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Zoe nodded slowly, as if she had been given a date for a test result.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.67,0:04:09.04,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Scott turned to the racks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.04,0:04:11.93,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He wanted the name more than he had wanted anything since the quay.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.93,0:04:20.91,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Something on this campus had brought a dozen machines down on a burning ship with Zoe in a boat under it, and had hunted her across a quad, and the only one in the room who knew what it was had just said, politely, that she
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.91,0:04:22.14,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}would rather not say.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.14,0:04:25.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He felt the stick warm a little in his hand, and he made himself breathe.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.07,0:04:28.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}And for a heartbeat he saw the hall from above.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.95,0:04:31.35,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was there and gone, like the light of a match.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.35,0:04:38.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He was looking down on it from somewhere high in the dark, over the racks, and the whole floor was laid out under him the way a battlefield had once been laid out under a hill.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.02,0:04:39.80,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The rows of green and amber lights.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.80,0:04:41.63,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The folded arms along the benches.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.63,0:04:44.50,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Sotiris small and lit by his phone, by the cooling plant.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.50,0:04:47.53,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Himself, an old man with a stick, very small.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.82,0:04:55.52,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}And Zoe, a step behind his left shoulder and a little to the side, standing with her hands in her coat pockets under the shutter.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.80,0:05:01.62,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then he was on the floor again, looking at the racks, and he knew without turning exactly where she stood.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.92,0:05:02.65,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He didn't turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.65,0:05:08.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He had seen it from above once before, a long time ago, on a field in the rain, and he had never written it down.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.87,0:05:10.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He didn't write it down now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.17,0:05:12.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"We're done," he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.17,0:05:14.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Thank you, Mr Malamas."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.42,0:05:20.88,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Out in the yard the cold came at them after the hall's dry warmth, and the sky was the white of winter afternoons.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.88,0:05:25.85,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}A short flight of concrete steps went down from the yard to the path behind the building.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.85,0:05:28.10,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Zoe stopped at the top.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.37,0:05:29.90,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then she took his arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.22,0:05:36.40,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She put her hand through it just above the elbow, the way people do on a stair, and held it, and they went down the steps together.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.40,0:05:40.57,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was the first time she had touched him in the open, where anyone at a window could see.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.57,0:05:42.52,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He felt it all the way through his coat.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.52,0:05:47.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He didn't say anything, because he was afraid that if he did she would remember she had done it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.52,0:05:49.95,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"It was careful with me," she said at the bottom.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.95,0:05:50.75,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Did you hear?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.75,0:05:52.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was being careful."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.72,0:05:53.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I heard."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.10,0:05:56.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Something that's careful with you knows who you are."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.92,0:05:58.45,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She didn't let go of his arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.45,0:06:02.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I'd like to know who it is that it's being careful for."
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.30,0:06:08.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Behind them the shutter began to come down on its motor, slowly, though nobody had touched it, and Scott looked back.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.15,0:06:19.75,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Under its falling edge he could see into the hall's dark, and down the racks, as the shutter closed, every status light blinked once, together, all the way along, like a breath held.
